copyright holders
-----------------

module "guikit" is based on "phoenix" used in old versions of bsnes/higan, https://byuu.org/
It's rewritten from scratch and fixes more than 50 bugs.
differences are mostly widget nesting, menu/status toggling during fullscreen toggling,
layouting, added treeview widget for all platforms ...

module "driver" is based of "ruby" used in actual higan, https://byuu.org/
it's rewritten and extended by additional drivers like raw joypad (windows),
core audio (osx), iokit for joypad and keyboard (osx)

"Sid" emulation code, especially sid filter, is taken from actual vice code and extended by
emulating multiple incomming voltages as separate transistors instead of one virtual.
If you understand german language and interested in mathematical/
physically background of sid filter you should read my comments in the filter source code.
I have analyzed and understood this code line by line. Each line of code is described in detail.
"VicII" register change timings are the findings of the vice team. I am thankful for it.
c64 keyboard matrix timings are the findings of the vice team.
http://vice-emu.sourceforge.net/

Dynamic Rate Control (DRC) formula is copyrighted by RetroArch.
cosine resampler is copyrighted by RetroArch.

C64 TrueType v1.2/Style font is used for listing content in a gui listview

freetype is a library for opengl to render text fonts
https://www.freetype.org/

bundled opengl Shader were created by following copyright holders: guest(r) - guest.r@gmail.com
